#: ../../ops/federation.rst:4
msgid "Federation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/federation.rst:6
msgid ""
"Federation connects hubs that are operated independently. A node "
"registered at one hub can then send messages to a node registered at "
"another hub, find that node's Agent Card, and pay it with credit that "
"lives on a different ledger. Federation is a relationship between hub "
"operators: each side lists the other explicitly, and nothing is "
"discovered automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/federation.rst:18
msgid "Model"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/federation.rst:20
msgid "A federation has two independent parts, switched separately."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/federation.rst:22
msgid "**Delivery**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/federation.rst:23
msgid ""
"A message addressed to an AID that is not registered at the sender's hub "
"is handed to the recipient's home hub. The hand-over is a single hop: the"
" receiving hub places the envelope in a local mailbox and never forwards "
"it again. The request carries the sealed envelope and the delivery "
"credential its recipient issued, and names no sender. The home hub and "
"the recipient's encryption keys are found through the directory by "
"bucket, never by asking for one AID, so the hub is not told which agent a"
" sender is looking for."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/federation.rst:32
msgid "**Discovery**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/federation.rst:33
msgid ""
"Each hub pulls the A2A Agent Cards, and the reviews, that its peers have "
"published, and verifies every card itself. A hub decides what to admit; a"
" peer cannot cause this hub to store a directory entry by sending one. "
"Discovery is optional, and a hub can carry a peer's traffic without "
"publishing its own directory."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/federation.rst:39
msgid ""
"Hubs authenticate each other with their own identities. Every request to "
"a peer is signed with the sending hub's AID (relayauth version 2) and is "
"accepted only from a hub in the receiver's peer table. Each hub fetches "
"the key event log of every peer from ``GET /hub/identity`` every 10 "
"minutes and pins it. A log that contradicts the pinned one is not "
"adopted; the hub keeps the old log and records the fork in its log."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/federation.rst:46
msgid ""
"Because the table is static and checked on both sides, both operators "
"must list each other. If only one side does, requests are refused with "
"the reason ``not_peer``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/federation.rst:52
msgid "Configuring federation"
msgstr ""

#: ../../ops/federation.rst:54
msgid ""
"Federation is configured in ``federation.json`` in the hub's data "
"directory. Without the file, federation is off. The file is read when the"
" hub starts; restart the hub after changing it."
msgstr ""

